<div class="mx-auto max-w-md pb-12">
  <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between">
    <h1 class="text-3xl text-gray-900">
      <%= @workout[:date].strftime('%A %b %-d') %>
    </h1>
    <a href="/workouts/<%= @workout[:id] %>" class="text-sm text-gray-500 underline hover:text-lime-500">record</a>
  </div>

  <%# Every tap inside this div replaces the whole of it, and an innerHTML swap empties
      the element before it refills it -- which drops the panel strip's scrollLeft to
      zero, because a scroll container with no content has nowhere to be scrolled to. Left
      alone that makes the swipe worse than the scroll it replaces: finishing a set on the
      third lift would land the lifter back on the first, on the one screen where their
      hands are busy. So the offset is read off the strip on the way out and put back on
      the way in.

      These two attributes are on the div rather than on any of the forms because this div
      is the one element on the screen htmx never replaces. A handler bound inside
      #session-body would be swept away by the first swap it handled, which is exactly the
      re-binding problem that kept a JS gesture library off this screen; both events reach
      here by bubbling. It restores the offset rather than a lift number so that a swap
      triggered from anywhere -- a rating, a revised weight, the session RPE below the
      strip -- leaves the strip where the lifter left it, mid-swipe included. %>
  <div id="session-body"
       hx-on::before-swap="this.dataset.stripScroll = this.querySelector('#lift-strip').scrollLeft"
       hx-on::after-swap="this.querySelector('#lift-strip').scrollLeft = this.dataset.stripScroll">
    <%= render('workouts/_session_body') %>
  </div>
</div>
